00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:27.667
and shed the weight of that

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.703
where she really just started to blossom.

00:09:30.703 --> 00:09:31.470
And I remember

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.371
hearing it

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:33.472
with her once

00:09:33.472 --> 00:09:34.574
when they were talking

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:35.641
about her new style,

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:38.077
when she kind of stepped into her own

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:38.844
and she was saying,

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:40.246
I'm tired of singing the blues.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.048
I want to sing rock and roll.

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:43.649
I want to I want to dance.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:44.216
I want you know,

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:46.652
she was free in a lot of ways.

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.888
And and you heard that in her voice.

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:50.222
You heard that in her music.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:53.092
I mean, so many people have so eloquently

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:55.828
been talking about how she was was,

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:56.228
you know,

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:58.264
the epitome of resilience,

00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:00.232
the epitome of a strong woman.

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:01.567
Not only was she

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:02.068
a mother

00:10:02.068 --> 00:10:03.002
and raised her children,

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:04.136
she raised the children

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.606
that I had before.

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:09.542
She was just kind of a mother to so many.

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:11.744
You know, Oprah Winfrey

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:13.346
she revered her as well,

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:14.280
one of her favorite

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:14.914
kind of a mother

00:10:14.914 --> 00:10:16.983
figure to her in so many ways.

00:10:17.483 --> 00:10:18.618
But she set the table

00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:21.020
for so many of these pop stars

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.521
that we see today.

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:24.557
And her story is just one

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:25.891
of strength and resilience.

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:28.160
I mean, there's no other way to put it.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.161
I, I heard Chloe

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:31.597
saying that she was one of the hardest

00:10:31.597 --> 00:10:33.032
working women in show business.

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:33.766
I would argue

00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:36.769
that she was the hardest working woman

00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:37.603
in show business.

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:39.305
And what we saw her story,

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:40.106
we saw it, of course,

00:10:40.106 --> 00:10:41.140
play out on the big screen

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:42.241
with Angela Bassett

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:43.609
so brilliantly portrayed her.

00:10:43.609 --> 00:10:45.511
And what's love got to do with it?

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:48.280
We saw her fight for everything

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.882
she ever had,

00:10:49.882 --> 00:10:51.951
and she fought down to the very end.

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:54.153
I mean, it's a very sad day

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:55.287
in the music world.

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:56.822
It's a sad day

00:10:56.822 --> 00:10:58.090
in American history

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.693
because she was a trailblazer in

00:11:00.693 --> 00:11:01.994
just about every avenue

00:11:01.994 --> 00:11:03.763
that she ever decided to take on.

